efore.bak\\n/lambda/nfs/whchoi/startup-patches/tiered-serve/cd3_current.sha256.20260901_route_before.bak\\n/lambda/nfs/whchoi/startup-patches/tiered-serve/serving_max_batched_tokens.patch\\n/lambda/nfs/whchoi/startup-patches/tiered-serve/serving_max_batched_tokens_from_1024.patch\\n/lambda/nfs/whchoi/startup-patches/tiered-serve/serving_performance_suite.patch\\n# CD3 startup patch backup\\n\\n- Generated: 2026-09-01 UTC\\n- Source repository: `/root/projects/tiered-serve`\\n- Source HEAD: `5d56a972bb80444671b9d27293e3fa18076c0d58`\\n- Consolidated patch SHA-256: `95ad90192897b34d11f79f0cbc541552a61346cacd60d99b01bfdeb2fecf0c92`\\n- Files changed: 27\\n\\n## Startup order\\n\\n1. `serving_max_batched_tokens.patch` (or its `from_1024` variant)\\n2. `serving_performance_suite.patch`\\n3. `apply_cd3.sh /root/projects/tiered-serve`\\n\\n`apply_cd3.sh` verifies and applies the consolidated `cd3_current.patch`.\\nIt is idempotent. The old two-stage patch files are retained only as rollback\\nartifacts and are not loaded at container startup.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis snapshot contains the current CD3 weight, fused-GEMM, KV codec, CPU\\nweight/KV encoders, benchmark, serving integration, model configuration, and\\nCD3 tests. Weight encode defaults to CPU; CUDA is used only to stage completed\\ncompressed buffers and for decode/fused-MM. The legacy GPU encoder is available\\nonly through the explicit debug override `TIERED_SERVE_CD3_WEIGHT_CPU_ENCODE=0`.\\nUnrelated working-tree changes were intentionally excluded.\\n\\nThe CPU KV encoder additionally contains the 2026-09-01 optimization set:\\n\\n- block-owner, single-source-pass encoding;\\n- min/max exception-free fast path;\\n- SVE2 predicate counting on the exception path;\\n- NEON hierarchical packing of 16 three-bit codes;\\n- uninitialized temporary exception scratch.\\n\\nDirect-to-persistent Packed20 packing was measured but not retained because it\\nwas 3–6% slower for medium and large batches.\\n\\nThe consolidated snapshot additionally contains:\\n\\n- host-native CD3 weight encoding with 64-row stripe parallelism;\\n- adaptive OpenMP team sizing for a single KV compression worker;\\n- batched NumPy KV slot allocation instead of a per-block Python loop;\\n- production fused-MM crossover calibration through N=128 on GH200.\\n- 128-thread standalone CD3 decode, with two logical chunks per thread;\\n- two half-width live output accumulators with the same two 128-bit stores,\\n  reducing standalone decode latency without changing the format;\\n- 2-D `(tile, block)` KV decode launch geometry;\\n- direct-to-cache indexed KV decode with no raw-BF16 intermediate copy;\\n- selected-run KV staging for partial restores below the slot high-water mark.\\n- one aligned slot-major CD3 blob and row-stride-aware CPU/GPU kernels;\\n- one `cudaMemcpyBatchAsync` submission for all K/V staging runs;\\n- cached block/slot device metadata and one native K/V decode dispatch.\\n- active-set identity/content caching with generation-safe invalidation;\\n- a dense steady-state decode plan that skips filtering, sorting and run scans.\\n- a fully CPU P4Flat weight post-process (blocked relayout and subtile codec),\\n  so CPU weight encoding no longer launches CUDA encode kernels;\\n- a frozen-split weight benchmark that separately reports H2D, resident GPU\\n  decode, and their combined latency.\\n- projection-specific fused-N calibration overrides, with a uniform override\\n  retained for compatibility;\\n- exact-length CD3 frozen-split staging views, so standalone fallback accepts\\n  variable-sized Packed20x3 exception streams;\\n- startup route reporting that reflects projection-specific overrides.\\n- a GH200/Llama-70B prefill weight-stream cutoff of N=1856: compressed\\n  standalone decode below the cutoff and raw BF16 transfer at or above it;\\n- an AST-level regression test that pins the calibrated CD3 cutoff.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- The old CD3 patch's complete path set is contained in this p